  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.71 P0-3 Required Semantic Delta Realization Seal makes the existing primary requiredDelta, mustAddBeyondKnown, and avoidReframeOnly fields explicit current-turn semantic completion criteria in the sole Generation contract. A required delta must add focus-relevant judgment, information, choice, or action not already supplied by recent conversation; rewording, regrouping, or relisting prior content cannot satisfy it, while NONE never manufactures novelty. No new field, planner, gate, judge, repair, retry, fallback, model call, role, domain, utterance, keyword, wording, length, list, or post-generation authority is introduced.';
  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.72 P0-5 R1.3 Acknowledgement Authority Execution moves the execution meaning of the existing Canonical acknowledgement selection from editable Role prose into the sole Generation semantic contract. selected=false consumes customer input inside the selected core contribution without creating an independent reception act; selected=true realizes only the already-selected relational function. Role and Identity Prompt remain the sole editable Persona HOW and no longer interpret internal acknowledgement fields. This adds no field, selection, role, domain, utterance, keyword, lexical rule, output quota, planner, gate, judge, repair, retry, fallback, model call, or post-generation rewrite.';
  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.73 P0-5 R1.3 Final Single-Branch Acknowledgement Execution compiles the acknowledgement state already derived from Canonical Acts into one current-turn execution branch before Generation. An unselected acknowledgement means every customer-visible semantic unit must realize or directly support a selected Act; a reception, evaluation, or paraphrase-only unit remains an unselected Act even when fused into the same sentence, paragraph, or HVE segment. Necessary customer facts may still serve as minimal premises inside the selected core reasoning. A selected acknowledgement retains only its existing relational function and required/optional necessity. This adds no field, selection, phrase list, role, domain, utterance, keyword, output quota, planner, gate, judge, repair, retry, fallback, model call, or post-generation rewrite.';
  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.74 P0-5 R1.4 Acknowledgement Semantic-Surface Boundary Correction removes the v1.72-v1.73 Runtime-authored acknowledgement execution branch and the duplicate model-facing acknowledgement false flag. Canonical Plan remains the sole owner of explicit required relational Acts; acknowledgement Acts already remain losslessly visible there, while ordinary incidental relationship wording is calibrated only by the persisted Role to Identity Prompt HOW authority. The revised default Role Prompt distinguishes useful relational function from routine evaluation by function rather than phrase, role, domain, or test sample. This is an Authority reduction: no new field, selector, planner, gate, judge, repair, retry, fallback, model call, output quota, lexical rule, or post-generation rewrite is added.';
  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.75 P0-5 R1.5 Persona Prompt Carrier and Direct-Contribution Calibration keeps the persisted Role to Identity Prompt chain as the sole editable HOW authority but compiles it once into a dedicated subordinate system Persona section instead of burying its text inside the large user-context JSON. The user-context transport removes the duplicate Prompt text while Final HumanTurn diagnostics retain the complete provenance. The revised default Prompt defines a useful opening by semantic effect: the visible response begins with the selected contribution itself; an understanding declaration, customer-expression evaluation, or answer-preview that can be deleted without changing judgment, information, choice, or next action is not a contribution. Direct conclusions and genuine emotion, relationship repair, misunderstanding resolution, or responsibility acknowledgement remain valid contributions. No phrase list, role/domain/test branch, new authority, planner, gate, judge, repair, retry, fallback, model call, output quota, or post-generation rewrite is introduced.';
  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.76 P0-5 R1.6 Decision-Relevant Delta and Existing Customer-Input Execution Calibration refines the same persisted Role Prompt HOW boundary so a scene summary, abstract principle, category label, or answer preview whose practical value is wholly supplied by following specifics cannot masquerade as the first contribution; a genuine conclusion or organizing judgment remains valid. The sole Generation WHAT contract also explains the already-projected selectedComponents.customerInput and completion semantics: no selected customer-input dependency means no new question or requested input, while ALLOW_CONTINUATION only leaves the conversation non-terminal and grants no Act by itself. This changes no Canonical selection, wording, length, segmentation, role/domain/test sentence, planner, gate, judge, repair, retry, fallback, model call, output quota, or post-generation path.';
  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.77 P0-5 R1.7 Current Execution and Historical Surface Authority Separation compiles only the already-selected current customer-input/completion branch into a salient system execution section instead of describing mutually exclusive branches around a buried user-context field. Raw prior assistant text remains exact lived continuity evidence, but is transported as a non-chat verbatim evidence record with no current surface authority; its wording, opening, order, length, and organization cannot become an implicit Persona example. Truncated diagnostic excerpts are structurally de-duplicated against their full raw assistant turn. The persisted Role to Identity Prompt remains the sole editable Persona HOW and is placed beside the current execution projection immediately before the protocol. This adds no phrase list, role/domain/test branch, current-turn selector, state, planner, gate, judge, repair, retry, fallback, model call, output quota, or post-generation rewrite.';
  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.78 P0-5 R1.8 Prompt Principle Consolidation freezes the v1.77 Runtime transport and replaces the system-recommended Role Prompt\'s repeated opening/acknowledgement calibration paragraphs with one shorter positive contribution-first principle plus one functional deletion boundary. Current customer facts, constraints, concerns, and observations are inputs to the answer rather than separate reception objects; direct conclusions and genuinely necessary emotional or relational contributions remain valid. Only Roles whose persisted Prompt exactly equals the newline-normalized v1.76 system default are adopted; authored Role and every Identity Prompt remain untouched. This is configuration reduction, not a new Runtime authority, phrase list, role/domain/test branch, selector, state, planner, gate, judge, repair, retry, fallback, model call, output quota, or post-generation rewrite.';
  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.79 P0-5 R1.9 Persona HOW Signal Reduction records the v1.78 user Live NO-GO and removes duplicated truth, permission, protocol, and implementation-boundary prose from the system-recommended Role Prompt. Those deterministic responsibilities remain in the existing Generation system contract; the persisted Role Prompt now carries only a short conversational HOW: continue from shared premises, begin with the actual answer, reserve explicit reception for a real emotional or relational function, and preserve speaker continuity. Exact adoption accepts only the v1.78 system default or its exact PC-persisted NFKC value; authored Role and every Identity Prompt remain untouched. No phrase list, role/domain/test branch, selector, state, planner, gate, judge, repair, retry, fallback, model call, output quota, or post-generation rewrite is introduced.';
  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.80 P0-5 R1.10 Functional Emotional Boundary Calibration records the v1.79 Live PARTIAL result and narrows one ambiguous exception inside the existing persisted Role Prompt: explicit reception is reserved for turns where emotional stabilization itself is part of the current task, or where relationship repair, misunderstanding resolution, or responsibility acknowledgement is actually needed. Ordinary consultations remain contribution-first even when the customer wording carries emotion. This replaces the prior broad emotional-response wording inside the same sole Role to Identity Persona HOW owner; it adds no second prompt, acknowledgement selector, phrase list, role/domain/test branch, planner, gate, judge, repair, retry, fallback, model call, output quota, or post-generation rewrite.';
  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.81 P0-3 Regression Canonical Completion Execution Boundary Convergence keeps the v1.69 P0-3 behavior baseline frozen and changes only the existing model-facing Current Canonical Execution projection after new v1.80 Live proved two execution misses: customerInput NOT_SELECTED could still be treated as conversational continuation, and a correctly selected NATURAL_CLOSE/STOP_AFTER_REQUIRED could still expand accepted prior content or reopen a service entry. ALLOW_CONTINUATION is now projected only as conversation-state truth, never as current-reply continuation permission; terminal completion explicitly ends the current generation after required Acts and keeps prior accepted content as continuity evidence rather than a new contribution. No Role/Identity Prompt, Canonical selection, Deep Recognition, output wording rule, role/domain/test branch, planner, gate, judge, repair, retry, fallback, model call, model parameter, output quota, or post-generation rewrite is introduced.';
  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.82 P0-3 Pre-Reply Exchange-State Temporal Demotion preserves the existing Conversation Reality exchange fact while renaming its ordinary Generation projection from exchangeState to exchangeStateBeforeCurrentReply. New Live proved a correctly selected NATURAL_CLOSE/STOP_AFTER_REQUIRED can still occasionally reopen a future service entry even when Canonical execution is explicit; source audit confirmed Role Posture/servicePresence remain diagnostic-only and the remaining model-facing ambiguity is that ONGOING describes the exchange state before this reply, not permission for this reply to continue. The same factual truth remains available for fresh/ongoing continuity, but it can no longer present as a competing current completion signal. No Role/Identity Prompt, R1 behavior, Canonical selection, Deep Recognition, Conversation Reality producer, role/domain/text rule, planner, gate, judge, repair, retry, fallback, model call, model parameter, output quota, or post-generation rewrite is introduced.';
  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.83 P0-5 R1.11 Embedded Evaluative Reception Functional Deletion Boundary reopens only R1 Persona HOW after cross-role Live showed a remaining semantic loophole: ordinary replies can fuse agreement, approval, correctness-confirmation, or comprehension reception into the first substantive sentence even when acknowledgement is absent and the customer premise is already shared. The same sole persisted Role to Identity Prompt evaluates that embedded reception by function, not vocabulary or position: if removing it changes no actual judgment, information, choice, action, emotional stabilization, relationship repair, misunderstanding resolution, or responsibility acknowledgement, it is omitted and the reply starts from real incremental value. Genuine factual certainty and genuinely needed emotional or relational work remain allowed. P0-3 v1.82 is frozen; no Runtime acknowledgement branch, lexical blacklist, role/domain/test branch, planner, gate, judge, repair, retry, fallback, model call, model parameter, output quota, or post-generation rewrite is introduced.';
  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.84 P0-5 R1.12 Given-Premise and New-Contribution Ownership Boundary records the v1.83 Live PARTIAL result: deletion-by-function alone still lets a customer-owned premise be relabeled as the model own factual judgment, especially when agreement or certainty is fused into a substantive sentence. The same sole persisted Role to Identity Prompt now distinguishes proposition ownership before surface realization. Facts, constraints, observations, preferences, decisions, and accepted directions already supplied by the customer or established context are reasoning premises and are implicit by default; they may be minimally surfaced only when omission would break reference or condition scope, or when that premise itself is the current confirmation, correction, or challenge target. Factual confidence and degree remain available for genuinely new model-owned judgments. The v1.80 emotional stabilization, relationship repair, misunderstanding resolution, and responsibility acknowledgement boundary is preserved unchanged. P0-3 v1.82, R2, R3, and Grounding remain frozen; no lexical blacklist, Runtime reception selector, role/domain/test branch, planner, gate, judge, repair, retry, fallback, model call, model parameter, output quota, or post-generation rewrite is introduced.';
  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.85 P0-5 R2.1 Active Constraint Decision Projection closes the existing CUSTOMER_CONSTRAINT producer-to-consumer gap without adding a new authority. The existing Deep Recognition call may emit explicit customer-owned decision constraints as STATE evidence; ConversationState persists exact quoted evidence under the current long-horizon task, task-scoped relevance keeps still-active constraints available across paraphrases, State Planning projects only currently relevant explicit facts, and existing Canonical Act.parameters.known consumes those facts alongside stated needs and preferences. FinalHumanTurn remains unchanged and losslessly carries the same Canonical Acts into the sole model-facing generation payload. No role/domain/product/location/utterance keyword rule, fixed ranking, second planner/gate/judge/repair/retry/fallback/model call, diagnostics send control, or delivery rewrite is introduced.';
  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.86 P0-5 R1 Regression Narrow Reopen plus R2.1 Decision-Integrity Observability preserves the v1.85 recommendation/state architecture while tightening only the sole persisted Role to Identity Persona HOW ownership boundary: a customer-owned premise cannot gain model-owned contribution status merely because the reply adds social reassurance, relationship-building normalization, or a prevalence/normality/reasonableness judgment that has no decision consequence. Such a judgment remains allowed when it is itself the information being asked for or changes the current answer. In parallel, Runtime diagnostics expose the already-existing R2.1 chain from recognized CUSTOMER_CONSTRAINT STATE evidence through relevant memory, canonical/state-guidance explicit facts, and Canonical Act known parameters. The diagnostic projection is read-only and has no generation, selection, final-candidate, delivery, or send-authority effect. No lexical blacklist, role/domain/product/test branch, second planner/gate/judge/repair/retry/fallback/model call, output quota, or post-generation rewrite is introduced.';
  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.87 P0-5 R1.14 Functional Preface Deletion Boundary restores one general function test inside the same sole persisted Role to Identity Persona HOW after v1.86 natural Live showed that proposition ownership alone can still leave a socially useful-looking but semantically unnecessary preface before the real answer. Any component is evaluated by current-turn function rather than wording or position: if removing it changes no actual judgment, information, choice, risk, or action and it does not perform an already-authorized emotional or relationship task, it is not new contribution and Generation should begin from the actual increment. Legitimate model-owned factual, degree, risk, prevalence, comparison, or recommendation judgments remain available when they materially answer the current turn. R2.1 recommendation/state behavior and its read-only diagnostics remain unchanged. No lexical blacklist, phrase-frequency rule, role/domain/product/test branch, Runtime selector, second planner/gate/judge/repair/retry/fallback/model call, output quota, or post-generation rewrite is introduced.';
  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.88 P0-5 R1.15 Canonical Reception Contribution Ownership plus R2.1 Natural Constraint Producer Robustness closes two Live-proven owner gaps without widening phase scope. For R1, Current Canonical Execution now projects whether the already-selected Canonical Plan contains an independent relational/reception Act; when it does not, Persona warmth may shape selected value Acts but cannot manufacture a separate acknowledgement, reassurance, normalization, approval, or relationship-maintenance contribution. A prevalence/normality/degree/comparison judgment remains allowed when it materially realizes an already-selected value Act. This is Canonical WHAT authorization, not a wording/order/length rule and not a lexical filter. For R2.1, the existing single Deep Recognition call now performs an explicit decision-space test over customer-owned current-message information, preserves qualifying constraints independently from current question/feedback semantics, declares the previously omitted recognizedItems.name schema field, and no longer drops an otherwise valid recognized item merely because descriptive name metadata is absent. Exact customer evidence, state persistence, task scoping, Planner known projection, diagnostics-only observability, and the existing primary plus JSON-repair call count remain unchanged. No keyword/domain/example branch, second planner/gate/judge/repair/retry/fallback/model call, diagnostic send control, output quota, or post-generation rewrite is introduced.';
  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.89 P0-5 R1.15 REFROZEN plus R2.1 Constraint Admission Precision Boundary records the cross-role natural Live result without changing R1 behavior: R1.15 is refrozen because unauthorized social-reception prefacing did not recur while legitimate answer-owned prevalence, degree, comparison, and risk judgments remained available. R2.1 keeps the v1.88 Recognition-to-State-to-Canonical-to-Planner-to-Decision chain unchanged and narrows only Deep Recognition admission. CUSTOMER_CONSTRAINT now requires two independent semantic qualifications inside the existing single Deep Recognition result: the proposition must already be established by the customer rather than being a question target, option under evaluation, feedback/acceptance, future-intent-only statement, or model inference; and changing/removing that established condition must materially alter decision space. The normalizer fail-closes CUSTOMER_CONSTRAINT items unless constraintBasis=CUSTOMER_ESTABLISHED and changesDecisionSpace=true. This is proposition-ownership plus decision-impact admission, not lexical/question-mark/domain/example logic. No R1 change, second planner/gate/judge/repair/retry/fallback/model call, diagnostics send control, delivery change, output quota, or post-generation rewrite is introduced.';
  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.90 P0-5 R2.1 SEALED plus R2.2 Choice Prioritization and Trade-off Ranking START records the v1.89 cross-role natural Live proof: true customer-established decision constraints remain durable through Recognition, State, Canonical Explicit Facts, Planning State Guidance and Decision Act known; question targets, acceptance/future-intent-only turns and close turns no longer over-persist as constraints. R2.1 is therefore SEALED and regression-only. R2.2 owner audit proves the existing Canonical recommendation Act already owns the current recommendation WHAT and receives current known constraints, while the mature Generation model owns candidate synthesis and natural choice realization. The exact delta sharpens only the existing recommendation decisionPurpose: when current conditions materially distinguish candidates, Generation must make the useful ordering visible instead of flattening materially inferior choices into peers, and a meaningful trade-off must be visible when the affected candidate is first recommended. Genuinely near-equal options and explicit comparison/listing requests may remain multi-option. Grounding proves candidate facts but cannot manufacture equal rank, ranking reasons, or a candidate quota. No fixed option count, rank-label template, phrase rule, role/domain/product/location/test branch, R1 change, second planner/gate/judge/repair/retry/fallback/model call, diagnostics send control, delivery rewrite, output quota, or post-generation rewrite is introduced.';
  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.91 P0-5 R1 Regression-only Cross-layer Reception Authority Seal plus R2.2 Choice Coverage/Projection Closure is limited to two new Live-proven defects. R1 reopens narrowly because value-only Canonical turns again produced premise-evaluating social reception even though acknowledgement=NONE and PRIMARY_FIRST; the Current Canonical Execution boundary now makes function ownership position-independent and explicit across Role/Identity HOW: without a selected reception Act, warmth/respond/hold-space semantics may shape a selected value Act but cannot create a proposition that evaluates the customer premise, concern, choice or situation when deleting that proposition leaves the actual selected answer unchanged. Legitimate answer-owned prevalence, degree, comparison, risk or normality judgments remain allowed when the judgment itself is required new domain/decision information. R2.2 no longer depends on responseTarget.focus=RECOMMENDATION to carry choice semantics: the existing DIRECT_ANSWER and PROVIDE_GENERAL_GUIDANCE value Acts receive the same conditional choice-prioritization purpose whenever their actual answer content contains multiple viable directions, while pure factual/single-conclusion turns must not manufacture options or ranking. Existing RECOMMEND_GROUNDED_ITEM ranking purpose is preserved through enrichActParameters instead of being overwritten, and DIRECT_ANSWER likewise preserves the Canonical purpose selected upstream. R2.1 remains SEALED; no lexical blacklist, phrase-frequency rule, role/domain/product/location/test-utterance branch, fixed option count/rank template, second planner/gate/judge/repair/retry/fallback/model call, diagnostic send control, delivery rewrite, output quota, or post-generation rewrite is introduced.';
  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.92 P0-5 R1 Regression-only Model-facing Semantic Contribution Scope plus R2.1 SEALED Precision Regression Closure keeps phase scope fixed after new v1.91 natural Live. R1 does not add a phrase rule or output filter: FinalHumanTurn now projects the existing Canonical Act selection as a structured receptionContribution authorization under canonicalPlan and exposes semanticContributionScope=SELECTED_CANONICAL_ACTS_ONLY. This closes the remaining same-sentence loophole by making function-level contribution scope model-facing: a fused proposition or modifier gains no authority merely because it is attached to a selected value Act; legitimate answer-owned factual, prevalence, degree, comparison, risk and choice judgments remain allowed when they materially realize that selected Act. R2.1 stays SEALED and reopens regression-only at producer admission: CUSTOMER_CONSTRAINT now requires a third orthogonal typed qualification, constraintRole=OPEN_DECISION_CONDITION, in addition to CUSTOMER_ESTABLISHED and material decision-space impact. Completed/accepted decisions remain DECISION_OUTCOME and purchase/try/execute intentions remain ACTION_OR_PURCHASE_INTENTION rather than being relabelled as constraints; existing DECISION and other state lanes retain their own semantics. R2.2 implementation is unchanged and remains Live pending. No lexical blacklist, phrase-frequency rule, role/domain/product/location/test-utterance branch, second classifier/planner/gate/judge/repair/retry/fallback/model call, diagnostics send control, delivery rewrite, output quota, or post-generation rewrite is introduced.';
  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.93 P0-5 R1 Regression-only Canonical Speech-Act Permit Convergence plus R2.1 Scoped-Key Normalization closes only the two latest Live-proven residuals. R1 replaces the accumulated reception explanation with one compact CURRENT_SEMANTIC_PERMIT derived exclusively from the already-selected Canonical Acts; FinalHumanTurn also marks Role/Identity generationGuidance as EXPRESSION_ONLY_NO_SEMANTIC_DELTA. The permit is exhaustive for customer-visible semantic speech acts: Persona may change wording, tone, emphasis and natural organization inside selected Acts but cannot add any separately functioning social or relational contribution that disappears under a neutral realization of the same selected Acts without loss of their actual value. This is function ownership, not phrase/position/length control. Read-only diagnostics now expose the exact generation kernel plus the same FinalHumanTurn permit so Live can prove deployment and model-facing authority without affecting generation, selection, candidate, delivery or send. R2.1 remains SEALED and changes only semantic-key hygiene: CUSTOMER_CONSTRAINT recognition canonicalizes any accidentally echoed constraint.<taskId>. scope back to the semantic key before the existing State owner scopes it once, preventing duplicate task prefixes without changing admission, evidence, memory relevance, Canonical, Planner or Decision semantics. R2.2 implementation is unchanged and remains Live pending. No lexical blacklist, phrase-frequency rule, role/domain/product/location/test-utterance branch, fixed option/rank/length/output quota, second classifier/planner/gate/judge/repair/retry/fallback/model call, diagnostic send control, delivery rewrite, or post-generation rewrite is introduced. V1.94 P0-5 R1.18 REFROZEN plus R2.1 regression closure and R2.2 Grounded Realization Convergence records the v1.93 cross-role Natural Live proof: value-only turns no longer create unselected social/reassurance contributions while selected NATURAL_CLOSE remains naturally relational; R2.1 no longer duplicates task scope and retains its sealed owner-chain. R2.2 ordinary choice/trade-off behavior is retained, while the remaining Grounded Live failure is fixed only at the existing service-realization projection: when Canonical already selected RECOMMEND_GROUNDED_ITEM or EXPLAIN_GROUNDED_FACT and actual grounded Knowledge is available, that selected grounded value Act becomes the realization carrier instead of being flattened behind an earlier generic DIRECT_ANSWER/PROVIDE_GENERAL_GUIDANCE Act. Required generic Acts remain losslessly present in canonicalPlan and must still be completed; when grounded Knowledge is absent the existing first-value fallback remains, so no grounded obligation can be manufactured. R2.2 is code-complete pending final grounded Natural Live before SEALED; R2.3 Response Effort / Depth Calibration is entered as the next owner-audit stage only and receives no surface/runtime implementation in this delta. No new planner, grounding selector, judge, repair, retry, fallback, model call, fixed candidate count/rank label, domain/phrase branch, diagnostic send control, delivery rewrite, or post-generation rewrite is introduced.';
  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.95 P0-5 final closure addresses only the two post-v1.94 Natural Live defects before R2.3. R1 reopens regression-only as Persona Semantic Leakage: the persisted Role to Identity Prompt chain remains the sole editable HOW source, but ordinary Generation now receives it as EXPRESSION_SOURCE_DATA_ONLY under a structured PERSONA_SEMANTIC_PROJECTION derived from the already-selected Canonical Acts. Raw Prompt text is no longer rendered as a free-standing imperative block: any Prompt instruction whose realization would require a customer-visible proposition or speech act outside selectedActTypes is INERT_THIS_TURN, and selectedReceptionActTypes=[] leaves warmth, patience and naturalness available only as expression qualities, not as reassurance, validation, congratulation, social-normalization or relationship-maintenance semantics. This is least-privilege Persona transport, not a lexical filter, second Persona, prompt rewrite, or output postprocessor. R2.2 closes Grounded Obligation Convergence at the existing Canonical recommendation owner: Grounding still cannot create a recommendation need, but when the Canonical Response Target is already RECOMMENDATION and matched entity-level Knowledge exists, RECOMMEND_GROUNDED_ITEM becomes REQUIRED for that same recommendation obligation rather than a dispensable PREFERRED second layer. The existing generic recommendation value remains selected and may fuse with the grounded candidate; Grounding only supplies candidate facts/provenance and does not create ranking reasons, fixed candidate counts, rank labels or output templates. v1.94 service-realization carrier logic remains unchanged. R2.1 stays SEALED; R2.3 remains NOT STARTED until post-fix Natural Live proves no R1 leakage and actual grounded candidate realization. No new planner, grounding selector, gate, judge, repair, retry, fallback, model call, domain/phrase branch, fixed length/count quota, diagnostic send authority, delivery rewrite, or post-generation rewrite is introduced.';
  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.96 P0-5 R1 regression-only Persona System-Channel Demotion and Unified Semantic Capability follows v1.95 Natural Live. Source audit proves Role Behavior, Account Voice, raw HumanTurn surface controls and Understanding unresolvedNeed remain server-side diagnostics/upstream context and are not ordinary model-facing Persona instruction channels, so they stay untouched. The remaining high-privilege path is the persisted Role to Identity Prompt raw text itself: v1.95 wrapped it as EXPRESSION_SOURCE_DATA_ONLY but still embedded that raw text inside the system message. v1.96 removes the raw persisted Prompt text from the system channel entirely. The system receives only one Canonical-derived PERSONA_SEMANTIC_CAPABILITY containing selectedActTypes, selectedReceptionActTypes and EXPRESSION_ONLY_NO_SEMANTIC_DELTA; the unchanged persisted Role/Identity Prompt is transported exactly once in Current Conversation Context as ordinary expression source data. No lexical sanitation, semantic rewriting, prompt classifier, second Persona, second model call, judge, repair, retry, fallback, post-generation rewrite, role/domain/product/location/test-utterance branch, or fixed length/count quota is added. R2.2 code remains byte-unchanged from v1.95 and continues to await a real RECOMMEND_GROUNDED_ITEM Natural Live; R2.1 remains SEALED and unchanged. The established-premise restatement issue observed in repeated wide-hip follow-ups is recorded only as a future R2.4 Contextual Extension and R2.5 Incremental Value acceptance case; it is not pulled into this R1 closure or R2.3 implementation.';
  generationKernelSeed.contentSeed += ' V1.97 P0-5 final pre-R2.3 closure follows the first v1.96 Natural Live that simultaneously re-proved the R1 residual and exercised the real grounded recommendation path. R1.21 Independent Acknowledgement Capability does not reopen Persona transport or add a wording blacklist: the existing Canonical semantic permit now exposes one explicit function-level independentAcknowledgement capability derived only from selected Canonical reception Acts. When no reception Act is selected it is NOT_AUTHORIZED, making base-model conversational initiative subject to the same exhaustive semantic permit instead of allowing an extra standalone social acknowledgement that can be deleted without loss of the selected value Acts. Legitimate answer-owned judgments that materially realize a selected value Act remain allowed, and NATURAL_CLOSE remains available through its own selected Act semantics. R2.2 Grounded Observability Convergence changes diagnostics only: v1.96 Live already proved Grounded Obligation REQUIRED, GROUNDED_FACT/GROUNDED_INFORMATION carrier, and a concrete merchant candidate in customer-visible text. The remaining CURRENT_TURN_GROUNDED_VALUE_MISSED is a false negative caused by requiring an extra lexical recommendation signal. The existing Output Act Recognizer now accepts, only inside an exact CANONICAL_SEGMENT_PLAN-bound RECOMMEND_GROUNDED_ITEM segment with matching allowed Grounding refs, a positive grounded entity assertion from those same refs as observed grounded candidate realization. Missing refs, boundary/uncertain clauses, or unbound text still cannot manufacture Grounding. R2.2 Generation remains unchanged; R2.1 remains SEALED and unchanged; R2.3 remains NOT STARTED until the post-v1.97 Natural Live gate passes. No new planner, selector, gate, judge, repair, retry, fallback, model call, lexical phrase requirement, diagnostic send authority, delivery rewrite, post-generation rewrite, or fixed length/count quota is introduced.';
